      "alignment_delta_seconds": -0.013208333333352584,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "N_CW and N_ACW chips detach from one branch and enter a formula workspace.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "section": "equation",
      "text": "Their difference is the numerator, and their total is the denominator.",
      "word_count": 11,
      "raw_file": "audio_v4/raw/s15-b20390383d0f.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "df34573da5f93f81196644456dd94b2387b503cbac0bb29dd3c0fb0def3ef0bf",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v4/decoded/s15.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "652d692d856d682d82ea1545d5eff8d98b82de4dbeff70068403c9b254975e6b",
      "audio_start_sample": 7051098,
      "audio_end_sample": 7249242,
      "audio_start_seconds": 146.897875,
      "audio_end_seconds": 151.025875,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 4407,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 146.9,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": 0.002125000000006594,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "The numerator and denominator build term by term around a fraction bar.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "section": "equation",
      "text": "The sign would indicate which label is more numerous, but the predeclared asymmetry value remains withheld.",
      "word_count": 16,
      "raw_file": "audio_v4/raw/s16-57707812688a.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "825ed198ea3e8b4b28d9016ef2b868b36e46a6f62052a70691739bc23ed6bb85",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v4/decoded/s16.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "a584356781b15b16dbf2fce7e872fe3441b8d4b9575e8ad494a82376b93d6b96",
      "audio_start_sample": 7285242,
      "audio_end_sample": 7550202,
      "audio_start_seconds": 151.775875,
      "audio_end_seconds": 157.295875,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 4553,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 151.76666666666668,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": -0.009208333333333485,
      "pause_after_samples": 157881,
      "pause_after_seconds": 3.2891875,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "A symmetric unselected sign rail appears; the symbolic equation completes and a value lock closes in the same state.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s17",
      "section": "controls",
      "text": "The control matrix joins the mirror, both thresholds, and same-object pairs.",
      "word_count": 11,
      "raw_file": "audio_v4/raw/s17-3d9085cd8f35.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "9b709db3ace5478cc321fc0cb21e79438e47e91f03461746d7866b8e96a18511",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v4/decoded/s17.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "0101f89181148582a15a849fb0c1290d8b3b53ae6e0aef5b5298d9f820095024",
      "audio_start_sample": 7708083,
      "audio_end_sample": 7970739,
      "audio_start_seconds": 160.5850625,
      "audio_end_seconds": 166.0570625,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 4818,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 160.6,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": 0.014937500000002046,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "Three control rows reveal: mirror, thresholds, paired same object.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s18",
      "section": "controls",
      "text": "They test inversion, threshold sensitivity, and individual change versus sample composition; design only.",
      "word_count": 13,
      "raw_file": "audio_v4/raw/s18-4d1afd6be2a8.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "d09d0dc12afa20d9401ca95e85c1e2d7b211193dfea4df2b5ff8884ef4a65e59",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v4/decoded/s18.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "660980cb14b4f995941c6f26c56e3e47e16728d14922488662930dba6f26bb4c",
      "audio_start_sample": 8006739,
      "audio_end_sample": 8345427,
      "audio_start_seconds": 166.8070625,
      "audio_end_seconds": 173.8630625,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 5004,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 166.8,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": -0.0070624999999893134,
      "pause_after_samples": 157880,
      "pause_after_seconds": 3.2891666666666666,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "Each control connects to its tested failure mode; DESIGN ONLY banner wipes across.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s19",
      "section": "discipline-gates",
      "text": "We tied our own hands so the answer cannot be shaped by choices made after seeing it.",
      "word_count": 17,
      "raw_file": "audio_v4/raw/s19-b62c1d547b78.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "540b561e9b600ed07f3d476409ba3cd89b41b859f2f18e89ed93dd0115ce3d2d",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v4/decoded/s19.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "1da9892d56c1e69baf3efac82303967ff5b806ff5177df8324277ea336a3ebc4",
      "audio_start_sample": 8503307,
      "audio_end_sample": 8754443,
      "audio_start_seconds": 177.15222916666667,
      "audio_end_seconds": 182.38422916666667,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 5315,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 177.16666666666666,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": 0.014437499999985448,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "A discipline seal closes around the full method while later-choice arrows are visibly blocked.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s20",
      "section": "discipline-gates",
      "text": "That standard makes the independent post-run verdict the next gate; the stored-direction frame and evidence, receipt, and referee checks must also meet the frozen rules.",
      "word_count": 25,
      "raw_file": "audio_v4/raw/s20-b1363e4835be.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "55f51022337e726938dd348ba84e1db9d805ede59147d58c3b0140b621ec084d",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v4/decoded/s20.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "37efbd3324c9375208e03b2a21e4f6406b4add18bba3666bc842d3867ac84b6f",
      "audio_start_sample": 8790443,
      "audio_end_sample": 9275435,
      "audio_start_seconds": 183.13422916666667,
      "audio_end_seconds": 193.23822916666666,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 5494,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 183.13333333333333,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": -0.0008958333333453083,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "Specific open review nodes appear as consequences of the self-imposed standard; a pulse stops before the answer field.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s21",
      "section": "boundary",
      "text": "Known now are the sample, estimator, mirror logic, and controls; no result value, direction, or interpretation is reportable.",
      "word_count": 18,
      "raw_file": "audio_v4/raw/s21-7356873d828a.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "b29facc7b4c9a2680195e6a59ff7cfc0ae45c7af237ee2eb4ccf91810b006a44",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v4/decoded/s21.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "5c4aba2f18947702ce9e6fd2046fd6791848d9e7ee187e2271f8d50d4ad47412",
      "audio_start_sample": 9311435,
      "audio_end_sample": 9741131,
      "audio_start_seconds": 193.98822916666666,
      "audio_end_seconds": 202.94022916666665,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 5820,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 194.0,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": 0.011770833333343944,
      "pause_after_samples": 157880,
      "pause_after_seconds": 3.2891666666666666,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "KNOWN and NOT REPORTABLE boundary columns build from the discipline diagram.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22",
      "section": "payoff",
      "text": "Ask the opening question again: images or labeling process?",
      "word_count": 9,
      "raw_file": "audio_v4/raw/s22-c6ceeafd1436.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "99eae27e3466204d5d7f33e30683871a84792cc895b1bbcfe686f2d471116f4d",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v4/decoded/s22.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "4e3bb656f34da2da2f5e8a7dc282bfc33cbf739d83728993e1192b1d70777182",
      "audio_start_sample": 9899011,
      "audio_end_sample": 10109827,
      "audio_start_seconds": 206.22939583333334,
      "audio_end_seconds": 210.62139583333334,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 6187,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 206.23333333333332,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": 0.003937499999977945,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "The exact two-explanation question returns above the completed mirror discriminant.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s23",
      "section": "payoff",
      "text": "Now we have a mirror test that forces those explanations to behave differently.",
      "word_count": 13,
      "raw_file": "audio_v4/raw/s23-4d2b901e7477.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "feff5c1666c6b0fae3d91caf8bbfa1dcdc13dd5ea72c9719999555e9127a82e4",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v4/decoded/s23.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "fc71025b08efadfff86cf374a5b67c1e0af3f60e45a73a98af04cfc0ac1a4f9e",
      "audio_start_sample": 10145827,
      "audio_end_sample": 10372771,
      "audio_start_seconds": 211.37139583333334,
      "audio_end_seconds": 216.09939583333335,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 6341,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 211.36666666666667,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": -0.004729166666663787,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "The mirror diagram reconnects both explanation lanes to a gated, still-empty answer field.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s24",
      "section": "payoff",
      "text": "Its gate-cleared answer is still missing; the scientific discriminant is not.",
